00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.710 align:start position:0%
 
you can't pause a movie on the big  screen but don't you wish you could  sometimes to get a better look at  batman's first big moment or to see all  the details in the riddler's hideout  keep watching for more pause-worthy the  batman moments  the opening sequence to the batman will  easily be one of the most talked about  scenes just because of the foreboding  tone it sets it's akin to the swelling  dread one feels as michael myers stalks  his prey in a halloween movie viewers  begin the film gazing through the eyes  of an enigmatic killer as he spies on  his victim the victim here is gotham's  mayor who sits unsuspecting in the  privacy of his luxurious abode as the  mayor views the public reaction to his  own campaign being broadcast on  television he's entirely unaware of the  danger that lurks in the shadows  hauntingly the figure of the riddler is  seen lying in weight not even five feet  away from his intended victim paul  dano's acting skill is on full display  here he can make your skin crawl with  just the movement of his eyes there's a  lot to savor in this sequence  particularly for viewers who have an  appreciation for horror themes and a  creepy atmosphere  the arrival of a film's title character  is often cause for a grand entrance  especially for a character as popular as  batman after the film moves on from its  horrifying introduction of the riddler  robert pattinson's bruce wayne speaks to  the audience via a sullen voiceover that  underscores the bleak and depressing  outlook of a city riddled with crime  while he's unsure whether he's actually  doing any good there is one thing he is  certain of criminals feel uneasy when  the bat signal shines in the sky and for  good reason  when that light hits the sky  [Music]  it's not just a call  it's a warning on a subway a gang that  looks to be inspired by the joker based  on their face paint targets an unlucky  soul and begins assaulting the poor man  quickly the sounds of footsteps can be  heard from within the dark tunnel  opposite the attackers the gang stops  and looks on waiting to see what emerges  from the dark as batman steps out into  the light he provides a demonstration of  his fear-inducing tactics by brutalizing  the gang's apparent leader in front of  them some stay and fight while others  flee it's a visceral display of batman's  rage and the scene earns its place as a  crowd-pleasing starting point for  batman's journey  long before the batman arrived in  theaters audiences knew for quite some  time that the penguin was going to have  a role in the film given that the story  takes place early in batman's  crime-fighting career the penguin isn't  quite yet the crime lord comics readers  know him to be he operates the iceberg  lounge under the mobbed-backed  supervision of carmine falcone colin  farrell absolutely disappears into the  penguin beneath prosthetics and makeup  work despite his altered appearance he  manages to nail the mannerisms of an ego  maniacal crook vying for power all the  fun begins when the dark knight heads to  the iceberg and questions the penguin  regarding his possible associations with  the recently deceased mayor seeing the  penguin and knowing that colin farrell  is buried beneath that grungy exterior  and slimy attitude is quite impressive  viewers might find themselves scanning  the character for any identifiable  aspect of the feral they remember but  they'll be hard-pressed to find anything  despite his own penchant for crime and  corruption the penguin positions himself  as one of the film's more interesting  characters even though he has little to  do with the burgeoning threat of the  riddler  throughout the film the riddler taunts  the residents of gotham with each kill  of course he believes that he's doing  the city a service by rooting out  corruption he also wants to get batman's  attention hoping that the vigilante will  side with him and his crusade to punish  the wicked i think i'm his last target  the news regularly shows recorded  threats that the riddler has posted in  an effort to gain clout and attention  throughout his campaign when the police  finally detain the riddler they  investigate his apartment which is  littered with newspaper clippings and  details of gotham's past and present the  riddler's cluttered abode contains  secrets and details that many fans will  certainly want to pause and scour for  clues to a larger world beyond gotham  city when the riddler discusses the  affluent wayne and arkham families  eagle-eyed fans can see a clipping  referencing edward elliott another  famous gotham city aristocrat those who  remember the elliott family from the  batman comics will recognize this as an  odd to tommy elliot bruce's former  childhood friend who grows up to become  the villainous hush  a batman movie just wouldn't be an epic  dark knight tale without a thrilling  batmobile sequence the batman doesn't  disappoint batman unveils his monster  machine with a thunderous rumble as the  dark knight pursues the penguin in an  effort to learn whether he's an  informant in a case the riddler keeps  referencing he has to deal with  dangerous criminals collateral damage  the penguin enters the freeway driving  the wrong direction dodging cars and  causing massive pileups at one point the  penguin causes a collision that includes  a truck carrying liquid fuel looking in  his rear view mirror he believes the  batman was either forced to stop his  pursuit or taken out in the explosion of  the truck's trailer he hollers for joy  i got you but his excitement is  short-lived as the batmobile comes  careening out of the flames much to the  penguin's horror hot rod enthusiasts who  love cards with some serious muscle and  fans of the batmobile will definitely  want to admire the stunt work and  thrilling visuals on display during this  harrowing sequence  the relationship between batman and  catwoman has long been one of the most  entertainingly complex in comics  although it is yet to be fully explored  on the big screen audiences have had  several opportunities to see the bat and  the cat in action michelle pfeiffer's  take on the role in 1992's batman  returns is unforgettable and anne  hathaway put her own spin on the  character when selena kyle fought side  by side with the caped crusader in the  dark knight rises the batman however  gives us what might be the most comics  accurate portrayal of catwoman yet with  zoe kravitz donning the leather bodysuit  and cat burglar mask when batman follows  selena to find out how she's involved in  the case at hand he discovers her  breaking into a safe commenting on her  uncanny ability to crack them so easily  startled she turns around and starts  fighting him the sequence fits neatly  into the narrative while doubling his  thrilling fan service for everyone in  the audience who's been looking forward  to seeing these characters come together  on screen again if viewers look closely  they can even see that selena is  sporting some wickedly long fingernails  primed for cat-like scratch attacks  thankfully the clash is brief just as  they have so many times before batman  and catwoman quickly form an alliance as  many viewers will no doubt suspect the  riddler's capture isn't the end but it  does set up his end game despite his  arrest he has power in the form of a  group of radical followers he's amassed  they detonate bombs he's planted on  gotham's reservoir walls causing a  devastating amount of water to pour into  the city when batman finally comes to  realize the riddler's terrible plot  fiery explosions can be seen erupting  throughout the city as seen reminiscent  of bane's assault on gotham in the dark  knight rises the results are horrifying  as residents of gotham clamor to reach  higher ground and water sweeps through  the streets the moment adds some serious  tension when audiences sit back and  realize that the riddler may have won  it's not often that the bad guy walks  away as the victor but this villain  managed to bring widespread destruction  to gotham the film's resolution settles  on batman understanding that he has to  do whatever he can to help gotham's  innocence in the face of unrepentant  evil  with the riddler locked up tight at  arkham he can no longer do any harm  directly but he's covered himself by  rallying extremists to his cause through  his online presence with gotham city  flooding and descending into mass panic  and chaos the group seeks to assassinate  a mayoral candidate and kill as many  people as they can at a political rally  the group positions themselves high up  on a rafter where they rain down a hail  of bullets upon the innocence below  batman once again makes a grand entrance  by demolishing the top of the building  with explosives and dropping onto the  rafter before engaging the riddler's  disciples the dark knight pummels and  defeats bad guy after bad guy in a  thrilling combat sequence still early in  his career batman isn't quite the near  perfect crime fighter we know he'll one  day become after recruiting years of  experience on the job he's attacked from  a blind spot and nearly falls off the  rafters surveying his surroundings he  employs the use of smoke to distract his  enemies while he takes each down one by  one  the batman establishes batman and  catwoman's relationship well both have  aided each other and even saved each  other's lives their paths are  interconnected and selena senses that  when she kisses the dark knight she  pleads with him to skip town with her  before realizing he's too fixated on  helping build a better gotham city while  she doesn't believe the city will ever  change that man has hope as the two set  off on their own paths they speed away  on their respective motorcycles despite  the scene coming at the tail end of the  film it's the first moment viewers can  admire the bat cycle in all of its  simplicity and beauty while bleak themes  of corruption and darkness pervade the  batman seeing the caped crusader and  catwoman racing down the road together  side by side offers a glimmer of hope  and optimism for the future even though  they ultimately go their separate ways  it's hard to believe selena kyle is out  of batman's life for good after all  they've been through together  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the batman are coming soon subscribe to  our youtube channel and hit the bell so  you don't miss a single one  [Music]  [Music]

